{"title":"Software Engineer Roadmap","role":"Software Engineer","summary":"A Software Engineer designs, develops, tests, deploys, maintains, and improves software systems. A Mathematics & Computing degree provides an especially strong foundation because it combines:","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Mathematics & Computing"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Software Engineer designs, develops, tests, deploys, maintains, and improves software systems. A Mathematics & Computing degree provides an especially strong foundation because it combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mathematics"},{"text":"Algorithms"},{"text":"Data structures"},{"text":"Computer science"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Computational thinking"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The graduate can work across:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Software development"},{"text":"Backend engineering"},{"text":"Full-stack development"},{"text":"Cloud engineering"},{"text":"Data engineering"},{"text":"AI/ML engineering"},{"text":"Systems engineering"},{"text":"Distributed systems"},{"text":"Cybersecurity"},{"text":"Quantitative computing"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The strongest positioning is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Strong Computer Science Fundamentals","Software Engineering","Problem Solving","Modern Development Tools"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Software Engineer can specialize in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Backend Engineering"},{"text":"Frontend Engineering"},{"text":"Full-Stack Development"},{"text":"Mobile Development"},{"text":"Cloud Engineering"},{"text":"DevOps"},{"text":"Distributed Systems"},{"text":"Data Engineering"},{"text":"Machine Learning Engineering"},{"text":"AI Engineering"},{"text":"Systems Programming"},{"text":"Security Engineering"},{"text":"Database Engineering"},{"text":"Platform Engineering"},{"text":"Developer Infrastructure"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Long-term roles can include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Software Engineer"},{"text":"Senior Software Engineer"},{"text":"Staff Engineer"},{"text":"Principal Engineer"},{"text":"Software Architect"},{"text":"Engineering Manager"},{"text":"Engineering Director"},{"text":"CTO"}]}]},{"heading":"Year 1 — Programming & Mathematical Foundations","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The first year should establish strong fundamentals rather than immediately jumping into frameworks."},{"type":"h","text":"Mathematics"},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Calculus"},{"text":"Linear algebra"},{"text":"Discrete mathematics"},{"text":"Probability"},{"text":"Statistics"},{"text":"Differential equations"},{"text":"Numerical methods"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Why Mathematics Matters"},{"type":"p","text":"Mathematics & Computing students should use their mathematical advantage for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Algorithm analysis"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"Machine learning"},{"text":"Cryptography"},{"text":"Computer graphics"},{"text":"Scientific computing"},{"text":"Quantitative systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Programming"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with one primary language."},{"type":"p","text":"Recommended:"},{"type":"h","text":"C++ / Java / Python"},{"type":"p","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Data types"},{"text":"Operators"},{"text":"Conditions"},{"text":"Loops"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Arrays"},{"text":"Strings"},{"text":"Pointers/references"},{"text":"Object-oriented programming"},{"text":"Exception handling"},{"text":"File handling"},{"text":"Do not learn five languages superficially."},{"text":"Become genuinely comfortable with one language first."}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Computer Science Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Start learning:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"C